          <groundspeak:date>2026-05-14T00:00:00Z</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="">L1ght3r</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="False">Found right after my track meet with Tnchrstn. TFTC!</groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="1361025672">
          <groundspeak:date>2026-05-14T00:00:00Z</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="">tnchrstn</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="False">I've been over here twice this week for my son's track meets. After he finished up this evening we stopped by here. This was a simple find but I was a little nervous because there's also a no trespassing sign in the yard. Second place I looked was where the cache was. Prior logs had me a little worried but the log was signable and there were only a few ants. Thanks for the cache!</groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="1360646516">
          <groundspeak:date>2026-05-12T00:00:00Z</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="">Sweet4aurora</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="False">Found it but couldn't sign the log way too wet. If you need verification that we found it, the log is so wet that it is transparent. Also there is a tiny bird inside and some kind of fungi growing inside.</groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
